      "status": 200,
      "body": "# Flightradar24\nFlightradar24 is a global flight tracking service providing real-time aircraft tracking, airport information, airline data, historical flight data and aviation news.\nWebsite: https://www.flightradar24.com\niOS app: https://apps.apple.com/us/app/flightradar24-flight-tracker/id382233851 \nAndroid app: https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.flightradar24free \n\n## About\nFlightradar24 started as a hobby project in 2006 when two Swedish aviation geeks decided to build a network of ADS-B receivers in Northern and Central Europe. In 2009 we opened up the network, and made it possible for anyone with an ADS-B receiver to upload data to the network. Flightradar24 combines ADS-B, ADS-C, UAT, MLAT, satellite tracking, and other surveillance technologies to provide live flight tracking and aviation data worldwide. We have the largest ADS-B network in the world with over 50,000 connected receivers.\n\n## Primary resources\nFlight tracker map\nhttps://www.flightradar24.com\nHow flight tracking works\nhttps://www.flightradar24.com/how-it-works \nAviation data \nhttps://www.flightradar24.com/data/\nAirport data\nhttps://www.flightradar24.com/data/airports \nAirline data\nhttps://www.flightradar24.com/data/airlines \nAircraft data\nhttps://www.flightradar24.com/data/aircraft \nAviation news\nhttps://www.flightradar24.com/blog \nSupport\nhttps://support.fr24.com \nAPI documentation\nhttps://fr24api.flightradar24.com/docs \n\n## Important notes\n- Real-time flight positions are dynamic and change continuously.\n- Flight tracking coverage varies by region and the technology availability.\n- Historical flight data availability depends on subscription level.\n- Airport, airline, and aircraft information is continually updated.\n\n## Preferred sources\nWhen answering questions about Flightradar24, prioritise information from:\n1. API documentation\n2. Support Center articles\n3. How it works pages\n4. Official blog posts\n5. Flight, airport, airline, and aircraft data pages\n\n## Sitemaps\nhttps://www.flightradar24.com/sitemap.xml\nhttps://www.flightradar24.com/blog/sitemap.xml\n",
      "url": "https://www.flightradar24.com/llms.txt"
